{
  "requirement": "`fingerprint` identifies the version of the contents. `format` renders that same value for the agent.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait NodeContents: Send + Sync {\n    fn fingerprint(&self) -> Fingerprint;\n    fn format(&self) -> String;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "Obligations derived from `requirements.sdk.graph.NodeContents`:\n1. `fingerprint` identifies the version of the contents. Equal contents should give equal fingerprints, and changed contents should give a different one.\n2. `format` renders that same value for the agent. It must describe the same retained contents that `fingerprint` identifies.\n3. The trait shape is `fn fingerprint(&self) -> Fingerprint`, `fn format(&self) -> String`, and `Send + Sync`.\n\nCoverage:\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[structural_fingerprint_example_tracks_the_selected_function]` covers the version-identity obligation.\n  - Reformatting the same function gives an equal fingerprint (`assert_eq!`).\n  - Changing the body from `allow()` to `deny()` gives a different fingerprint (`assert_ne!`).\n  - The same test asserts `format()` for all three variants: the original text, the reformatted text with its own layout, and the changed text. So `format` follows the same selected value that `fingerprint` identifies.\n  - It also coerces `&original` to `&dyn NodeContents` through `shareable<T: Send + Sync + ?Sized>`, which checks that the trait is object-safe and `Send + Sync`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[selected_contents_outlive_handles_and_later_file_edits]` covers the coupling between `format` and `fingerprint`.\n  - `format()` equals `\"second\"`, the selected text.\n  - The fingerprint value equals `structural_hash`, and its scheme is the language scheme plus `:own-v1`.\n  - After the source file is overwritten and the original handle is dropped, `fingerprint()` still equals the earlier fingerprint and `format()` still returns `\"second\"`. So both methods describe the same retained version.\n  - A fresh `from_id` after the edit fails, which confirms the file really did change.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks that the SDK's exported inventory matches the specification.\n- Other generic-bound checks exist (`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs`). They are not needed for this judgment.\n\nI found no requirement-violating behavior that these assertions would accept, and no missing scenario for a named obligation.",
